# Bot1 holds two Firestorm Phoenixes and casts one; on their next turn the opponent's Lightning Bolt kills it in their
# upkeep and it returns to their hand. Its effect is about that card alone (the ruling: "that particular card can't be played
# before your next turn begins, but a different Firestorm Phoenix in your hand can", CR 400.7): the opponent sees one
# Phoenix of the two in that hand, and a Phoenix may still be cast - the other one - with mana to spare.

[Bot1 Deck]
Firestorm Phoenix
Firestorm Phoenix
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mountain
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Firestorm Phoenix.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Firestorm Phoenix)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand = Firestorm Phoenix; Firestorm Phoenix; Mountain; Mountain
! Bot1.Hand.Firestorm Phoenix.Cast(Mana: short)

[Expect]
Bot2.Sees.Bot1.Hand = Firestorm Phoenix
Bot2.Sees.Bot1.Hand.Count = 1
